EXT. FLOATING MARKET OF THE LANTERN SEA - DUSK

Hundreds of boats lashed together on a windless lagoon. Paper lanterns hang from masts. Traders call across the water in a tangle of tongues. Drifting steam smells of spice and rain.

At the heart of the market, on a barge strung with silver bells, five figures stand in a ring.

QUEEN-MOTHER OSHUN ADEBAYO-LUMINARA (70s, sea-silk robe, crown of coral) holds a trident in one hand and a small carved box in the other.

Her son, PRINCE TAMSIN LUMINARA-VOSS (30s, silver armor, bloodshot eyes), stands stiffly at her right.

The sorceress NERISSA KALOMBO-AQUILA (40s, indigo cloak, hair braided with shells) waits on her left.

An old pirate captain, BARNABAS "BLACK BARNEY" OYELOWO-SMYTHE (60s, one eye, huge laugh), leans on a cutlass.

And the ferryman's daughter, PIPPA TRELAWNEY-ANAYA (14, barefoot, bright), clings to a mast.

OSHUN
(into the crowd)
Friends. Neighbors. Traders of the Lantern Sea. I have called you here to end the feud.

Silence ripples across the boats. Bells chime softly.

TAMSIN
Mother, this is unwise.

OSHUN
It is overdue.

NERISSA
It is a trap.

OSHUN
It is a truce.

BARNABAS
(booming)
Truce! I love a truce. When do we eat?

PIPPA
(whispering from the mast)
Captain Barney, hush.

BARNABAS
I can't hush. I'm a pirate.

OSHUN
Barnabas. Your fleet will withdraw from the northern channel.

BARNABAS
My fleet will think about it.

OSHUN
Your fleet will withdraw.

BARNABAS
(grinning)
Of course, Majesty.

NERISSA
And the sorcerers' guild?

OSHUN
Will return the stolen tides.

NERISSA
They were not stolen. They were borrowed.

OSHUN
For three centuries.

NERISSA
It was a long loan.

TAMSIN
Mother, enough.

OSHUN
Silence, Tamsin.

She opens the carved box. Inside rests a pearl the size of a fist, dull and grey.

OSHUN (CONT'D)
This is the Heart of the Lagoon. It has been dying for forty years. Unless all of you swear on it, it dies tonight.

Gasps ripple. Tamsin steps forward and seizes the box. Barnabas draws his cutlass. Nerissa raises a hand and the water around the barge begins to rise. Pippa leaps from the mast and lands between them all.

PIPPA
(shouting)
Stop it! All of you!

They freeze. Cutlass. Hand. Hand on the box. The lanterns sway.

PIPPA (CONT'D)
(quietly)
My father says a pearl dies when it stops being held.

OSHUN
Child--

PIPPA
So hold it. Together.

A long moment. Then Tamsin lowers his hand. Barnabas sheathes his cutlass. Nerissa lets the water fall. Oshun, tired, extends the box. One by one, they each place a hand on the pearl.

The grey surface warms. A faint pulse of silver rises, then gold, then every color the lanterns carry.

The crowd exhales. The boats begin to rock gently, as if the lagoon itself had sighed.

BARNABAS
(under his breath)
Well, I'll be.

NERISSA
It has been a long time since it glowed.

TAMSIN
(to Oshun, softly)
Forgive me, Mother.

OSHUN
There is nothing to forgive. Hold the light.

PIPPA
Can I go home now?

BARNABAS
(roaring with laughter)
She wants to go home! The savior of the sea wants to go home!

OSHUN
(smiling)
Pippa Trelawney-Anaya, you may go anywhere you like.

Pippa grins, drops from the barge into a small skiff, and begins to row, the lanterns blooming on the water around her.
